# nodeskip-one-pick: the skip takes a layer with one pick too (`picks == 0`
# becomes `picks <= 1` in TierCard::send_layer). Red: the unit test's layer 7
# (one pick) sends no frame, so `a_node_free_layer_sends_no_frame` sees one
# frame, not two; on a load the picked expert is served by nobody, so the
# stage card's wait of the layer never passes and the step names the tier a
# lost card (B11's bits differ or the clause fails by name).
--- a/crates/gpu/src/host/tier.rs
+++ b/crates/gpu/src/host/tier.rs
@@ -2295,7 +2295,7 @@
         row: usize,
         picks: u64,
     ) -> Result<bool, GpuError> {
-        if picks == 0 {
+        if picks <= 1 {
             // Nothing of the layer's is the node's to compute: the node is
             // sent no frame, so no round trip, and the host signals the
             // layer's unit itself ([`TierPage::add_unit`]).
